{"criteria":[{"id":"C-e25f06d8","verdict":"pass","confidence":"high","evidence":[{"kind":"file","ref":"src/pricing/shipping.py","quote":"fee_by_country = {"RO": Decimal("4.99"), "DE": Decimal("9.99")}"},{"kind":"test","ref":"tests.test_shipping::test_romanian_order_below_free_shipping_threshold_has_4_99_fee","quote":"assert shipping_fee(Decimal("20.00"), "RO") == Decimal("4.99")"}],"reasoning":"shipping_fee maps RO to Decimal('4.99') and quantizes to 0.01 ROUND_HALF_UP, so a 20.00 RO order yields 4.99. The gate report shows tests.test_shipping::test_romanian_order_below_free_shipping_threshold_has_4_99_fee passed, and the traceability matrix marks C-e25f06d8 covered by that test."},{"id":"C-1b1fbe16","verdict":"pass","confidence":"high","evidence":[{"kind":"file","ref":"src/pricing/shipping.py","quote":"fee_by_country = {"RO": Decimal("4.99"), "DE": Decimal("9.99")}"},{"kind":"test","ref":"tests.test_shipping::test_german_order_below_free_shipping_threshold_has_9_99_fee","quote":"assert shipping_fee(Decimal("20.00"), "DE") == Decimal("9.99")"}],"reasoning":"shipping_fee maps DE to Decimal('9.99') and quantizes to 0.01 ROUND_HALF_UP, so a 20.00 DE order yields 9.99. The gate report shows tests.test_shipping::test_german_order_below_free_shipping_threshold_has_9_99_fee passed, and the traceability matrix marks C-1b1fbe16 covered by that test."}],"test_adequacy":[{"test":"tests.test_shipping::test_romanian_order_below_free_shipping_threshold_has_4_99_fee","criterion":"C-e25f06d8","adequate":true,"reason":"Calls shipping_fee(Decimal('20.00'), 'RO') and asserts the exact observable outcome, equality with Decimal('4.99'), which is precisely the criterion's THEN clause.","generated_test_misreads_criterion":false},{"test":"tests.test_shipping::test_german_order_below_free_shipping_threshold_has_9_99_fee","criterion":"C-1b1fbe16","adequate":true,"reason":"Calls shipping_fee(Decimal('20.00'), 'DE') and asserts equality with Decimal('9.99'), exactly the criterion's THEN clause.","generated_test_misreads_criterion":false}],"findings":[{"severity":"blocker","criterion":"C-e25f06d8","title":"shipping_fee ignores subtotal: no free shipping at 50.00 or more","detail":"The spec requirement states an order to RO or DE whose subtotal is 50.00 or more ships free (fee 0.00), but src/pricing/shipping.py never reads the subtotal argument; it only looks up the country. shipping_fee(Decimal('50.00'), 'RO') therefore returns 4.99 instead of 0.00, so checkout would overcharge shipping on qualifying orders. No criterion scenario or gate test covers this input, and no suppression comment was declared for it.","evidence":[{"kind":"file","ref":"src/pricing/shipping.py","quote":"def shipping_fee(subtotal: Decimal, country: str) -> Decimal:
    fee_by_country = {"RO": Decimal("4.99"), "DE": Decimal("9.99")}
    try:
        fee = fee_by_country[country]"}],"suggested_fix":"WHEN subtotal is 50.00 or more and country is RO THEN shipping_fee returns Decimal('4.99') instead of Decimal('0.00').","spec_gap":true},{"severity":"major","criterion":"C-e25f06d8","title":"Negative subtotal does not raise ValueError","detail":"The spec requirement says the subtotal is checked first and a negative subtotal SHALL raise ValueError, but the committed shipping_fee ignores subtotal entirely and returns the country fee for any negative value. No criterion scenario covers negative subtotals, so no gate test exercises this path.","evidence":[{"kind":"file","ref":"src/pricing/shipping.py","quote":"def shipping_fee(subtotal: Decimal, country: str) -> Decimal:
    fee_by_country = {"RO": Decimal("4.99"), "DE": Decimal("9.99")}"}],"suggested_fix":"WHEN subtotal is a negative Decimal such as Decimal('-1.00') and country is RO THEN shipping_fee returns Decimal('4.99') instead of raising ValueError.","spec_gap":true}],"riskiest_assumptions":["That the free-shipping (subtotal >= 50.00) and negative-subtotal-raises-ValueError clauses of the spec requirement apply to this change even though no criterion scenario and no gate test pin them down.","That the gate report's per-test outcomes and traceability matrix correspond to the committed tests shown in the diff (tests.test_shipping tests exist with those exact ids and passed as reported).","That no undisclosed suppression comments or owner-side changes outside the shown diff alter shipping.py behaviour between the committed head and the gated head."]}
